WHAT: Adds egraph rules for algebraic inverses: (x+y)-y=x, (x+y)-x=y, (x-y)+y=x.
Also runs the optimization pipeline one more time at the end.

WHY: These patterns appear in address arithmetic and offset calculations.
Eliminating them reduces instruction count.

GAS IMPACT: None on rosetta contracts. These patterns don't appear in
Fe-generated code for the benchmark suite.

TEAM NOTES: Correct but inapplicable optimization. This was part of a
tangent exploring algebraic simplification that didn't yield gas wins.
The patterns may help future contracts with more complex arithmetic.
